 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Double function of the attributive Partizip II",
     "texto": [
      "1. **With transitive verbs (with haben)**: it has a **passive and resultative** meaning. The noun receives the completed action: **die gelieferten Sensoren** (the delivered sensors), **die beschädigte Dichtung** (the damaged seal).",
      "2. **With intransitive verbs of change or movement (with sein)**: it has an **active and completed-action** meaning: **der angekommene Zug** (the train that has arrived), **die gesunkenen Kosten** (the costs that have fallen).",
      "It is never used with intransitive verbs that take «haben» and express duration (**das geschlafene Kind* is not acceptable in formal German)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Verb type",
     "columnas": [
      {
       "texto": "Attributive example",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Equivalent analytic paraphrase",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      }
     ],
     "filas": [
      [
       {
        "texto": "Passive transitive",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
